{"content":[{"c":["ATHBASH*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Hebrew cryptograph in which the first letter of the Hebrew alphabet is substituted for the last, the second for the next-to-last, etc., to produce a code. Such a code or cipher was used for the word “Chaldea” in ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.51.1","r":"Jer.51.1","rawR":"Jer.51.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.51.1","value":"Jer.51.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jeremiah 51:1"}," (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," interprets the cipher as meaning “them that rise up against me”). Another athbash was used for “Babylon” in ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.25.26","r":"Jer.25.26","rawR":"Jer.25.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.25.26","value":"Jer.25.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jeremiah 25:26"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.51.41","r":"Jer.51.41","rawR":"Jer.51.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.51.41","value":"Jer.51.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"51:41"}," (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," treats that cipher as a proper name, “Sheshach”). The early Greek translation of the OT, the Septuagint, correctly deciphered these and translated them as “Chaldea” and “Babylon” respectively."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Athbash","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jeremiah 51:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.51.1","rawQueryValue":"Jer.51.1","sourceRefExact":"Jer.51.1"},{"anchorText":"Jeremiah 25:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.25.26","rawQueryValue":"Jer.25.26","sourceRefExact":"Jer.25.26"},{"anchorText":"51:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.51.41","rawQueryValue":"Jer.51.41","sourceRefExact":"Jer.51.41"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"1c5988b9f5e7166fb428ee89b7397be8f365506f3fdb7c8aa60751c86c1cf5f6","sourceItemName":"Athbash","sourceItemOrder":602,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Athbash","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Athbash*","title":"Athbash*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}